  "term": "stridor dentium",
  "definition": "Stridor dentium is an old term for grinding or gnashing the teeth. In this source, it refers especially to tooth-grinding seen in epilepsy and other convulsive disorders from spasm of the lower jaw muscles, and also to grinding caused by peripheral nervous irritation.",
